  "$schema": "../../schemas/ship.schema.json",
  "id": "falcon",
  "name": "Falcon",
  "manufacturer": "Solo & Sons",
  "role": "pirate",
  "description": "Long, low and built to be the last thing a hauler sees. Her radiator vanes reach forward like talons, and by the time they glow it is too late to run.",
  "credits": {
    "authors": [
      "Witchspace contributors"
    ],
    "license": "CC-BY-SA-4.0",
    "aiAssisted": true,
    "notes": "Original Witchspace geometry: a blade of a hull with a dorsal spine, and radiator vanes swept forward like talons (no wings: there is no air to fly on). A nod to CMDR Solo, who flew Elite in 1984 and draws its ships for Traveller. Scaled up by half in October 2026: at Cobra length she read as a sliver beside the traders she hunts."
  },
